      "message": "Yes pasting the reasoning based on inquiry from: b/172484781\n\n1) when sim card power off, if SIM card remove, What are the required values in the framework?\n\u003e\u003e CARDSTATE_ABSENT (nothing else populated)\n2) and If same sim card or other sim card inserted again, what are the required values in the framework?\n\u003e\u003e if sim card is re-inserted by user, or a new sim card is inserted, then this is a signal that they want to use it, and we should at least pop-up a UX asking if they want to use it (or automatically enable it). Hence in this scenario, we can power the sim card up normally. it does not have to stay in a power-off state, and we would expect the typical sim data population.\n\nWDYT? We kind of consider it a \u0027wipe\u0027 of power mode setting if the SIM card is physically removed and re-inserted.",
